# Name the product in one object's crops (the identity channel, CMB-112).
# crops: one to max_views RGB8 or BGR8 crops of the SAME object, ideally from different
# viewpoints; they are voted. barcode_images: optional close-range images of the barcode panel.
# The reply never forces a guess: STATUS_ABSTAIN says the channels cannot name one product,
# STATUS_UNKNOWN says there is positive evidence it is not a registered product, and it is also
# what a node without a loaded sidecar answers (sidecar_available = false).
# The SKU is the registry's internal product id: the GTIN for a product that has one (so every
# SKU exposed before product ids existed is unchanged), "prod-<hex>" for a product with no
# barcode. gtin/has_gtin give the product's GTIN when it has one; an empty gtin never means a
# GTIN. Barcode-less products are named by embedding and OCR only. The barcode channel can be
# disabled on the node (parameter barcode_enabled); barcode_enabled in the reply says whether it
# was, and channels_used lists the channels that ran. This service only reports; SKU write-once
# semantics stay in world state, which decides whether to accept it.

sensor_msgs/Image[] crops
sensor_msgs/Image[] barcode_images
---
uint8 STATUS_IDENTIFIED=0
uint8 STATUS_ABSTAIN=1
uint8 STATUS_UNKNOWN=2

uint8 status
bool sidecar_available
bool has_sku
string sku
bool has_gtin
string gtin
string reason
# One entry per piece of evidence, in parallel arrays: kind is embedding, ocr or barcode.
# evidence_product_ids is the product the evidence points at (what sku is compared with);
# evidence_gtins is that product's GTIN, "" when it has none.
string[] evidence_kinds
string[] evidence_product_ids
string[] evidence_gtins
float32[] evidence_scores
string[] channels_used
bool barcode_enabled
string backend_name
string backend_version
string registry_sha256
string calibration_sha256
float32 latency_ms
